{
  "title": "Cross-entropy loss",
  "function": "cross_entropy_loss",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "logits",
      "type": "vec"
    },
    {
      "name": "label",
      "type": "int"
    }
  ],
  "returns": "float",
  "library": true,
  "hints": [
    "The loss is −ln(softmax(logits)[label]). But don't compute the softmax and then take its log: a probability that rounds to 0 gives ln 0 = −∞.",
    "Use the identity ln softmax(z)ₖ = zₖ − log_sum_exp(z). Your `log_sum_exp` is already stable.",
    "Check 0 ≤ label < len(logits), then return log_sum_exp(logits) − logits[label]."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0
        ],
        0
      ],
      "description": "a 50/50 guess costs ln 2",
      "expected": 0.6931471805599453
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          2,
          1,
          0.1
        ],
        0
      ],
      "description": "the right class has the highest score: small loss",
      "expected": 0.41703001627783376
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          2,
          1,
          0.1
        ],
        2
      ],
      "description": "the right class has the lowest score: big loss",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 2.3170300162778337
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          1000,
          0
        ],
        1
      ],
      "description": "confidently wrong: huge but finite loss",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 1000.0
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          5,
          0,
          0
        ],
        1
      ],
      "description": "confidently right: tiny loss",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 0.020012253359626975
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        3
      ],
      "description": "a label past the last class must be rejected",
      "expect_error": true,
      "hidden": true
    }
  ]
}
